    "text": "Yes, an effective education system should weave together the three components highlighted\u2014right understanding (content), fulfillment in relationships (process and social engagement), and physical facility (resources and infrastructure). Presently many curricula emphasize content knowledge while under\u2011investing in relational dynamics and adequate material support, which limits holistic development and well\u2011being. The way forward is to design curricula that embed inquiry\u2011based learning (promoting right understanding), collaborative and community\u2011oriented projects (fostering relational fulfillment), and equitable access to learning environments, technology, and health resources (ensuring physical facility). This integrated approach aligns knowledge acquisition with social and material well\u2011being, preparing learners for continuous happiness and prosperity.",
